You can actually do something kind of similar on a real table if you're
going for a bank shot and don't hit at enough of an angle.  We used to
have competitions to see how many cross banks you could hit
intentionally and pocket the object ball (we used a side pocket),
getting more than 4 is pretty tough.

It doesn't help much in 8-ball, though, since you have to call which
pocket you're going for or it's not a legal shot in both American (APA)
and world (WPA) rules.



